### **Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)**
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Nighttime Parking Lot with Vehicle and Open Door Indicator" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :vehicle1 ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Vehicle parked in parking lot with open rear door" .

:evidence1 a :OpenDoorIndicator ;
    :description "Open rear door of vehicle detected" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1 .

:weather1 a :NightCondition ;
    :description "Low-light conditions in parking lot" .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision risk due to open vehicle door in parking lot" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :DistractionRisk ;
    :description "Driver distraction risk due to open door in low-visibility conditions" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.60"^^xsd:float .
```

